nginz: new per-location option `forward_oauth_z_client`. On locations that set it, nginz forwards a caller-supplied `Z-Client: Calendar` header (and only that value) to the upstream when the request has no connection (OAuth bearer callers); zauth access tokens keep the token's client. The default `nginx_conf` enables it on the meeting mutation routes so calendar integrations' `Z-Client: Calendar` reaches galley. If you override the nginz `nginx_conf.upstreams.galley` locations, add `forward_oauth_z_client: true` to `/meetings$`, `/meetings/([^/]*)/([^/]*)$`, its `/invitations`, `/invitations/delete` and `/link/refresh` sub-paths.
